<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xar Moron River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Shara Muren, Xilamulun River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shira-muren">Xar Moron</a> is a river of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and the main upper branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-river">Liao River</a>. Its basin, with that of the Laoha River, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Khitan, where they founded their capital Shangjing, and earlier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> cultures such as Hongshan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xar-moron-river.jpg" alt="Xar Moron River" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kmusser · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liaorivermap.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
